WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
OK.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.080
Welcome back.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.370
Let's get right into audience questions, first
one.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.290
David, if Biden gets elected in November,
what do progressive next?

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.830
So disclaimer, disclaimer, don't put the cart
before the horse.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.059
Everybody's got to go vote.

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:15.640
There is no guarantee that Joe Biden is going
to get elected.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.050
Republicans are certainly planning some October
surprises.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.689
We don't even know what they are yet.

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:25.640
But certainly claiming victory over coronavirus
may be an emergency.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.750
Use the vaccine, maybe more lies about economic
numbers.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.769
Who even knows?

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:32.810
But do not put the cart before the horse.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:35.500
Every single one of us needs to go out and
vote.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.140
Here is the analogy I've been using to talk
about a possible Biden victory over Trump.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.280
Biden winning doesn't score as many points.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.020
Biden winning gives us the ball back.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.300
We've been playing defense the entire time.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.960
Trump has been president.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:55.670
So if we get the ball back, that's when we
have to then put together our strategy for

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.090
how to put some points on the board.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:04.020
Now, this reminds me of the importance of
getting control of the Senate and maintaining

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:10.050
control in the House because Joe Biden is
not the most progressive candidate, but he's

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:16.420
not likely to veto legislation that makes
it through the House and Senate.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:19.190
Now, the devil is in the details there.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:20.870
You might imagine something like Medicare
for all.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.680
And you might say Biden would veto Medicare
for all.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.040
He says he's not for it.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.170
Well, Medicare for all is not going to pass
the Senate.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.170
Right.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.170
That's what you.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.170
And this is not.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.450
Don't attack the messenger.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.950
Even many Democratic senators don't support
Medicare for all.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:38.980
And if the Democrats get a majority in the
Senate, it would be a small one, maybe with

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.690
53 or 54 senators.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:44.729
Medicare for all is not going to make it to
Joe Biden's desk.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:47.750
So let's let's not let's think of, you know,
more realistic examples.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.160
And Virginia is a very realistic example.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:56.030
You've got a moderate Democratic governor
with a Democratic legislature and they've

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.729
gotten progressive things done.

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:03.080
And we've seen Virginia move to the left significantly,
even with a moderate Democratic governor.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.229
But like I've said before, a Biden win is
the start.

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:12.450
So extend House control, hopefully take control
of the Senate.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.790
And then in the immediate.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:20.870
Joe Biden needs to be pressured to reverse
the insane Trump executive orders that have

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:25.060
accumulated while Donald Trump has been in
the Oval Office and then the House and Senate

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.400
need to go to work.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.470
Biden is going to have to be pushed and he's
going to have to be pushed hard.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:35.540
And what I've been trying to communicate for
some time now is even if Biden isn't as progressive

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:42.030
as Bernie and he's nowhere near as progressive
as Bernie Sanders, Biden is running on what

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:46.060
if he were elected president, would be the
most progressive platform that a sitting president

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.060
has had.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.180
Just think through this, right.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.600
Biden is accused by many of being barely a
centrist.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.390
There's people say this guy's almost like
a moderate Republican.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.459
If you look at Biden's tax plan the way I
did on Monday this week, it's well to the

00:03:00.459 --> 00:03:01.930
left of Barack Obama's.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:06.630
If you look at the things that are in Biden's
tax plan, abolishing the lower rate for capital

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:15.180
gains, dramatically expanding the Social Security
tax on people earning above four hundred thousand

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:20.130
dollars a year, eliminating the stepped up
basis, I mean, there's not even a what what

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.530
Joe Biden wants to do tax wise as well to
the left of Barack Obama.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:29.400
If you look at Biden's health care plan, it's
obviously not Medicare for all, but it is

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.530
Obamacare.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:34.910
Plus a bunch of stuff to the left of Obama,
including Biden has said he would be supportive

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.990
of lowering the age for Medicare and a bunch
of other things.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.360
It is not Medicare for all.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:45.460
But the point is, if Biden gets it done, what
he wants to do would be the left most position,

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.750
public option, etc..

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:52.130
It's about what Obama started from, which
is public option with more stuff like lowering

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.930
the Medicare age.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.349
Biden supports the Green New Deal as a framework.

00:03:56.349 --> 00:04:01.500
And that is something that I mean, Green New
Deal wasn't even a term back then.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:06.629
So my point is not that Biden is the uber
progressive hero.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:14.080
My point is Biden has already made it clear
that if he were president, his policy would

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:19.359
be the most progressive of anyone who has
been president, not who has run.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.359
OK.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.959
And he's got to be held to it.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:25.979
And he has to be given the ability through
the House and Senate to actually get things

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:26.979
done.

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:30.080
And that's why if Biden gets elected, we've
gotten the ball back.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:30.830
That's when the offense starts

